  "why": "The statement bundles the original conjecture with unnamed generalisations, so even the 2008-2011 proofs of the elliptic-curve case and the Hilbert/Bianchi extensions are cases, not the whole. All are pre-snapshot. After the snapshot: Fu-Lau-Li-Xi (function-field Kloosterman) and Shi-Weng (high-rank zetas, not the L-function of E) are analogues, so variant. Goodson-Hoque was the close call: it computes Sato-Tate groups for a new family, but by the record the equidistribution is stated as already known from earlier CM theorems (Johansson; Banaszak-Kedlaya), so the paper settles no new case of the conjecture; I scored it none rather than case. Gallese-Goodson-Lombardo computes groups only, Vladuts assumes the conjecture, and the murmuration and point-count papers do not bear on it. No event credits an AI system with mathematics; the He-Lee-Oliver ML classifier and the 2026 'AI-assisted' murmurations paper name no system and prove nothing about Sato-Tate.",
